              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            While the field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            clearly originates in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            regarded up to topological
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"}> point-set topology
            ”), but only in topological spaces regarded up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            – hence it is interested only in the “weak
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} groups
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
            of the (weak)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of topological spaces but do not detect their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            class.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of topological spaces obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+category"} forcing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            to become
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            is the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"}> classical homotopy category
            ”
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            not to become plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure (short for “category of models for
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
          %h2#BackgroundOnTopologicalHomotopyTheoryFromAlgebraicTopology Topological homotopy theory
          %p
            This section recalls relevant concepts from actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"}> point-set topology
            ”) and highlights facts that motivate the axiomatics of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ModelCategoryTheory"} below
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
            and lemma
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#TheClassicalModelStructureOfTopologicalSpaces"} further below
          %p
            %strong Literature
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn15"}> Hirschhorn 15
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            between them. Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            are the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
          %p
            (Further
            %a{:href => "#ModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"} below
            we restrict attention to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
          %h3#universal_constructions Universal constructions
          %p
            To begin with, we recall some basics on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"} universal constructions
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+objects"} exponential objects
          %p Generally, recall:
          #LimitsAndColimits.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_\bullet
                    \\;\colon\;
                    I \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i \overset{\phi}{\longrightarrow} j)
                    \\;
                    \\mapsto
                    ( X_i \overset{X(\phi)}{\longrightarrow} X_j)
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
              over this diagram is an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              equipped with morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i \colon Q \longrightarrow X_i
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi i
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; Q
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{p_i}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{p_j}}
                    \\\
                    X_i &amp;&amp; \underset{X(\phi)}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; X_j
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Dually, a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-cone"} co-cone
              under the diagram is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              equipped with morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_i \colon X_i \longrightarrow Q
              such that all these triangles commute:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi q
                                    %mi i
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi q
                                    %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X_i &amp;&amp; \overset{X(\phi)}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; X_j
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{q_i}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{q_j}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; Q
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              over the diagram is a universal cone, denoted
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} X_i
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \longrightarrow \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} X_i
            %p
              Dually, a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over the diagram is a universal co-cone, denoted
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} X_i
          %p
            We now discuss limits and colimits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}=
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          #InitialAndFinalTopologies.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_i = (S_i,\tau_i) \in Top\}_{i \in I}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              be a bare
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi S
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{S \stackrel{f_i}{\to} S_i \}_{i \in I}
                  a set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  out of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+topology"} initial topology
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi initial
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{initial}(\{f_i\}_{i \in I})
                  is the topology on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimum"} minimum
                  collection of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
                  such that all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi initial
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i \colon (S,\tau_{initial}(\{f_i\}_{i \in I}))\to X_i
                  are
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                        %mi S
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{S_i \stackrel{f_i}{\to} S\}_{i \in I}
                  a set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  into
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+topology"} final topology
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi final
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{final}(\{f_i\}_{i \in I})
                  is the topology on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximum"} maximum
                  collection of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
                  such that all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi final
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i \colon X_i \to (S,\tau_{final}(\{f_i\}_{i \in I}))
                  are
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
          #TopologicalSubspace.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a single topological space, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_S \colon S \hookrightarrow U(X)
              a subset of its underlying set, the initial topology
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi initial
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{initial}(\iota_S)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InitialAndFinalTopologies"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi initial
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota_S
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (S, \tau_{initial}(\iota_S))
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    X
            %p
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              inclusion.
          #QuotientTopology.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Conversely, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_S \colon U(X) \longrightarrow S
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi final
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{final}(p_S)
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topology"} quotient topology
          #DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \colon I \longrightarrow Top
              be an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              (a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              to
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi i
