                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{k-1}
              by attaching cells precisely only of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              Strictly speaking a relative cell complex, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalCellComplex"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
              %em together
              with its cell structure, hence together with the information of the pushout diagrams and the transfinite composition of the pushout maps that exhibit it.
            %p
              In many applications, however, all that matters is that there is
              %em some
              (relative) cell decomposition, and then one tends to speak loosely and mean by a (relative) cell complex only a (relative) topological space that admits some cell decomposition.
          %p
            The following lemma
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations"}
            below are the only two statements of the entire development here that involve the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+particular"} concrete particular
            nature of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"}> point-set topology
            ”), everything beyond that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            homotopy theory.
          #CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Assuming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} subspace
              of a topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell complex
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalCellComplex"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of cells.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn15"} Hirschhorn 15, section 3.1
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              be a topological cell complex and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow Y
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} subspace
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P \subset Y
            %p
              by
              %em choosing
              one point in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
              of the intersection with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              of each cell of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              that intersects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              It is now sufficient to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              has no
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accumulation+point"} accumulation point
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compactness
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              does have an accumulation point, and hence the lack of such shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              and hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              intersects the interior of finitely many cells of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              To that end, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
              be any point. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              is a 0-cell in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi c
