                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              says, in view of the definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a map with the property that given a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              is also called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
              for maps whose domain is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-disk"} n-disk
            %p
              More generally one may ask functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              to have such
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
              for functions with arbitrary domain. These are called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibrations"} Hurewicz fibrations
          #SerreFibrationsByLiftingAgainstMapsHomeomorphicToDiskInclusions.num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              The precise shape of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n \times I
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              turns out not to actually matter much for the nature of Serre fibrations. We will eventually find below (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingPropertyInTheClassicalModelStructureOnTopologicalSpaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n \hookrightarrow D^n \times I
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              (lemma
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsAreRelativeCellComplexes"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalHomotopyEquivalencesAreWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
            %p
              But for simple special cases this is readily seen directly, too. Notably we could replace the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-disks"} n-disks
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              with any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              topological space. A choice important in the comparison to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              (
              %a{:href => "#GeometricRealizationSection"}> below
              ) is to instead take the topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-simplices"} n-simplices
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Delta^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; E
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id,\delta_0)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\times I &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Other deformations of the
              = succeed "-disks" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-disk" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (D^n \times \{0\})\cup (\partial D^n \times I) &amp;\simeq&amp; D^n
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    D^n \times I &amp;\simeq&amp; D^n\times I
                    }
            %p
              and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a Serre fibration equivalently also if it admits lifts in all diagrams of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (D^n \times \{0\})\cup (\partial D^n \times I) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; E
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id,\delta_0)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    D^n\times I &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            The following is a general fact about closure of morphisms defined by lifting properties which we prove in generality below as prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}
          #SerreFibrationHasRightLiftingAgainstJTopRelativeCellComplexes.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              (see remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfMorphisms"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              (def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingAcyclicCofibrations"}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalCellComplex"}
          %p
            The following statement is foreshadowing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequences+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequences of homotopy groups
            (
            %a{:href => "#LongSequences"}> below
            ) induced by any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
            %a{:href => "HomotopyFiberSequences"} below
            (example
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LongExactSequeceOfHomotopyGroups"}
          #SerreFibrationGivesExactSequenceOfHomotopyGroups.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \longrightarrow Y
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \colon \ast \to Y
              be any point and write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi y
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ι
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_y \overset{\iota}{\hookrightarrow} X \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} Y
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
              inclusion over that point. Then for every choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon \ast \to X
              of lift of the point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_{\bullet}(F_y, x)
                    \\overset{\iota_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_\bullet(X, x)
                    \\overset{f_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_\bullet(Y)
            %p
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
              is canonically identified with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_\ast
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ker(f_\ast) \simeq im(\iota_\ast)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_\ast
              is in the kernel of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
              (every sphere in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi y
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_y\hookrightarrow X
              becomes constant on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              For the converse, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha]\in \pi_{\bullet}(X,x)
              be represented by some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon S^{n-1} \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha]
              is in the kernel of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
