              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha'
              factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi y
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi ι
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_y\overset{\iota}{\hookrightarrow} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha'] = [\alpha]
              is in the image of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_\ast
          %p
            The following lemma
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
            above, are the only two statements of the entire development here that crucially involve the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+particular"} concrete particular
            nature of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"}> point-set topology
            ”), everything beyond that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            homotopy theory.
          #AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_5 Lemma
            %p
              The continuous functions with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RightLiftingProperty"}
              against the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi Top
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top} = \{S^{n-1}\hookrightarrow D^n\}
              of topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+cofibrations"} generating cofibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingCofibrations"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakHomotopyEquivalenceOfTopologicalSpaces"}
              as well as
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibrations"} Serre fibrations
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p We break this up into three sub-statements:
            %p
              %strong
                A)
                = succeed "-injective" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \hat X \to X
              have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ∃
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1}  &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; \hat X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_n}}\downarrow &amp;{}^{\mathllap{\exists}}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              We check that the lifts in these diagrams exhibit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(f)
              as being an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              on all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyGroupsOftopologicalSpaces"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
              the existence of these lifts says that every point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is in the image of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(\hat X) \to \pi_0(X)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjective
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo *
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0 = \ast \coprod \ast \longrightarrow \hat X
              be a map that hits two connected components, then the existence of the lift says that if they have the same image in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(X)
              then they were already the same connected component in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(\hat X)\to \pi_0(X)
              is also
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injective
              and hence is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            %p
              Similarly, for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \to \hat X
              represents an element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(\hat X)
              that becomes trivial in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(\hat X) \to \pi_n(X)
              has trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              and so is injective.
            %p
              Finally, to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(\hat X) \to \pi_n(X)
              is also surjective, hence bijective, observe that every elements in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X)
              is equivalently represented by a commuting diagram of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \hat X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X &amp;=&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              and so here the lift gives a representative of a preimage in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n}(\hat X)
            %p
              %strong
                B)
                = succeed "-injective" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}
            %p
              By an immediate closure property of lifting problems (we spell this out in generality as prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SaturationOfGeneratingCofibrations"}
              below) an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective morphism
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsAreRelativeCellComplexes"}
              = succeed "-injective" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
            %p
              %strong
                C) Acyclic Serre fibrations are in particular
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"} injective morphisms
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn15"}> Hirschhorn 15, section 6
              ).
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
              be a Serre fibration that induces isomorphisms on homotopy groups. In degree 0 this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an isomorphism on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo =
                            %mi ∅
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{-1} = \emptyset &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    D^0 = \ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              (this is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(f)
              being surjective) and in every commuting square of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^0  &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_0}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    D^1 = \ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              (this is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(f)
              being injective). Hence we are reduced to showing that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
              every diagram of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1}  &amp;\overset{\alpha}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_n}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    D^n  &amp;\overset{\kappa}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p has a lift.
            %p
              To that end, pick a basepoint on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n-1}
              and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              for its images in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              Then the diagram above expresses that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast[\alpha] = 0 \in \pi_{n-1}(Y,y)
              and hence by assumption on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              it follows that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha] = 0 \in \pi_{n-1}(X,x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa'
              making the upper triangle of our lifting problem commute:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi κ
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1} &amp;\overset{\alpha}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_n}}\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\kappa'}}
                    \\\
                    D^n
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              It is now sufficient to show that any such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa'
              may be deformed to a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho'
              which keeps making this upper triangle commute but also makes the remaining lower triangle commute.
            %p To that end, notice that by the commutativity of the original square, we already have at least this commuting square:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ι
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mi κ
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1} &amp;\overset{\iota_n}{\longrightarrow}&amp; D^n
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_n}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f \circ \kappa'}}
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\underset{\kappa}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This induces the universal map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\kappa,f \circ \kappa')
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
              in the top left, which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              (see
              %a{:href => "Top#TopologicalnSphereIsPushoutOfBoundaryOfnBallInclusionAlongItself"} this
              example):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ι
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi po
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mi κ
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi κ
                                %mo ,
                                %mi f
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi κ
                                %mo ′
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1} &amp;\overset{\iota_n}{\longrightarrow}&amp; D^n
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_n}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;(po)&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f \circ \kappa'}}
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\underset{\kappa}{\longrightarrow}&amp; S^n
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp; \searrow^{(\kappa,f \circ \kappa')}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This universal morphism represents an element of the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [(\kappa,f \circ \kappa')]
                    \\in
                    \\pi_n(Y,y)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a weak homotopy equivalence, there is a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\rho] \in \pi_{n}(X,x)
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_\ast [\rho] = [(\kappa,f \circ \kappa')]
            %p hence on representatives there is a lift up to homotopy
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ρ
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ⇓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi κ
                                %mo ,
                                %mi f
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi κ
                                %mo ′
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp;{}^{\mathllap{\rho}}\nearrow_{\mathrlap{\Downarrow}} &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    S^n
                    \&amp;\underset{(\kappa,f\circ \kappa')}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Morever, we may always find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\rho', \kappa')
              for some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho' \colon D^n \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa'
              to the reverse of
              = succeed ".\u201D)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            %p Consider then the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi κ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^n \overset{(f\circ \rho', \kappa)}{\longrightarrow} Y
            %p and observe that this represents the trivial class:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi κ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi κ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi κ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi κ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi κ
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mrow
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi ρ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi κ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi κ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi κ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi κ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi κ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi κ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    [(f \circ \rho', \kappa)]
                    \&amp; =
                    [(f\circ \rho', f\circ \kappa')]
                    +
                    [(f\circ \kappa', \kappa)]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = f_\ast \underset{= [\rho]}{\underbrace{[(\rho',\kappa')]}}
                    +
                    [(f\circ \kappa', \kappa)]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = [(\kappa,f \circ \kappa')]
                    +
                    [(f\circ \kappa', \kappa)]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = 0
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p This means equivalently that there is a homotopy
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \; \colon \; f\circ \rho' \Rightarrow \kappa
            %p
              fixing the boundary of the
              = succeed "-disk." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p Hence if we denote homotopy by double arrows, then we have now achieved the following situation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi ρ
                                %mo ′
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo ⇓
                                  %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1} &amp;\overset{\alpha}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_n}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;
                    {}^{\rho'}\nearrow_{\Downarrow^{\phi}}
                    \&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              and it now suffices to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              may be lifted to a homotopy of just
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho''
              is the desired lift.
            %p
              To that end, notice that the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon D^n \times I \to Y
              fixes the boundary of the
              = succeed "-disk" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
