            %h6#lemma_11 Lemma
            %p
              The construction in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory"}
              is indeed well defined.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_18 Proof
            %p
              First of all, the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi Q
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P Q X
              is indeed both fibrant and cofibrant (as well as related by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
              of weak equivalences to
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
