          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67, I.1 theorem 1
            )
          #ProofOfUniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory.proof
            %h6#proof_19 Proof
            %p
              First, to see that that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_{P,Q}
              indeed takes weak equivalences to isomorphisms: By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagrams"} commuting diagrams
              shown in the proof of lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConstructionOfLocalizationFunctorForModelCategoryIsWellDefined"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi Q
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P Q f
              is a weak equivalence if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mo ≃
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Q
                                    %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Q
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi P
                                  %mi Q
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mi y
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Q
                                    %mi Y
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mi Q
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{p_X}{\longleftarrow}&amp; Q X &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{j_{Q X}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; P Q X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{Q f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{P Q f}}
                    \\\(
                    Y &amp;\underoverset{p_y}{\simeq}{\longleftarrow}&amp; Q Y &amp;\underoverset{j_{Q Y}}{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp; P Q Y
                    }
            %p
              With this the “Whitehead theorem for model categories”, lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WhiteheadTheoremInModelCategories"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi Q
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P Q f
              represents an isomorphism in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              Now let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C}\longrightarrow D
              be any functor that sends weak equivalences to isomorphisms. We need to show that it factors as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi F
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi γ
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi ρ
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ho
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C} &amp;&amp; \overset{F}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; D
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\gamma}}\searrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\rho}&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\tilde F}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; Ho(\mathcal{C})
                    }
            %p
              uniquely up to unique
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_{P,Q}
              is the identity on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of fibrant-cofibrant objects. It follows that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F
              exists at all, it must satisfy for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{f}{\to} Y
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              both fibrant and cofibrant that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde F([f]) \simeq F(f)
                    \\,,
            %p
              (hence in particular
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mi Q
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F(\gamma_{P,Q}(f)) \simeq F(P Q f)
            %p
              But by def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
              that already fixes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F
              on all of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(\mathcal{C})
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F
              there exists any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              filling the diagram above.
            %p
              To that end, apply
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              to the above
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              to obtain
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mi iso
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi iso
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Q
                                    %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi P
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi Q
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi P
                                  %mi Q
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi iso
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Q
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Q
                                    %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi iso
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi P
                            %mi Q
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    F(X) &amp;\underoverset{iso}{F(p_X)}{\longleftarrow}&amp; F(Q X) &amp;\underoverset{iso}{F(j_{Q X})}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F(P Q X)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{F(f)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F(Q f)}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F(P Q f)}}
                    \\\
                    F(Y) &amp;\underoverset{F(p_y)}{iso}{\longleftarrow}&amp; F(Q Y) &amp;\underoverset{F(j_{Q Y})}{iso}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F(P Q Y)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here now all horizontal morphisms are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi X
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_X \coloneqq F(j_{Q X}) \circ F(p_X)^{-1}
              makes the required natural isomorphism:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi iso
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mi X
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi iso
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Q
                                    %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi P
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mrow
                                %mi P
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi P
                                  %mi Q
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mover
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi P
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi Q
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mi y
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                              %mi iso
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Q
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Q
                                    %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi iso
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi P
                            %mi Q
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mrow
                                %mi P
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\rho_X \colon &amp; F(X) &amp;\underoverset{iso}{F(p_X)^{-1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F(Q X) &amp;\underoverset{iso}{F(j_{Q X})}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F(P Q X)
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    \\tilde F(\gamma_{P,Q}(X))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{F(f)}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F(P Q f)}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\tilde F(\gamma_{P,Q}(f))}
                    \\\
                    \\rho_Y\colon&amp; F(Y) &amp;\underoverset{F(p_y)^{-1}}{iso}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F(Q Y) &amp;\underoverset{F(j_{Q Y})}{iso}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F(P Q Y)
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    \\tilde F(\gamma_{P,Q}(X))
                    }
                    \\,.
          #EssentialUniquenessOfLocalizationFunctorOfModelCategory.num_remark
            %h6#remark_13 Remark
            %p
              Due to theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
              we may suppress the choices of cofibrant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              and fibrant replacement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory"}
              and just speak of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+functor"} localization functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
