          %h2#TheClassicalModelStructureOfTopologicalSpaces The model structure on topological spaces
          %p
            We now discuss how the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            satisfies the axioms of abstract homotopy theory (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"}> model category
            ) theory, def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
          #ClassesOfMorhismsInTopQuillen.num_defn
            %h6#definition_37 Definition
            %p
              Say that a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong classical weak equivalence
                  if it is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakHomotopyEquivalenceOfTopologicalSpaces"}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong classical fibration
                  if it is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong classical cofibration
                  if it is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
                  (rem.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfMorphisms"}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalCellComplex"}
            %p and hence
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong acyclic classical cofibration
                  if it is a classical cofibration as well as a classical weak equivalence;
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong acyclic classical fibration
                  if it is a classical fibration as well as a classical weak equivalence.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi cl
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Fib
                      %mi cl
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Cof
                      %mi cl
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_{cl},\;Fib_{cl},\;Cof_{cl}
                    \\subset
                    Mor(Top)
            %p for the classes of these morphisms, respectively.
          %p
            We first prove now that the classes of morphisms in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassesOfMorhismsInTopQuillen"}
            satisfy the conditions for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure, def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
            (after some lemmas, this is theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
            below). Then we discuss the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
            (
            %a{:href => "#TheClassicalHomotopyCategory"}> below
            ) and then a few variant model structures whose proof follows immediately along the line of the proof of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
          %ul
            %li
