              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#BrownRepresentabilityTraditional"}> thm.
              ) implies that all additive reduced cohomology theories are degreewise representable this way (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#AdditiveReducedCohomologyTheoryRepresentedByOmegaSpectrum"}> prop.
              ).
          %h2#TheSuspensionLoopingDiscussion The suspension/looping adjunction
          %p
            We conclude this discussion of classical homotopy theory with the key statement that leads over to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory – 1
          #SuspensionAndLoopAreAdjointOnHomotopyCategory.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_49 Proposition
            %p
              The canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LoopingAsFunctorOnHomotopyCategory"}
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+pointed+homotopy+category"} classical pointed homotopy category
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalModelStructureOnPointedTopologicalSpaces"}
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Ω
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi Σ
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Sigma \dashv \Omega)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Ho(Top^{\ast/})
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\Sigma}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{\Omega}{\longrightarrow}}
                    Ho(Top^{\ast/})
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, this is equivalently the adjoint pair of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunctionInducesAdjunctionOnHomotopyCategories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi Maps
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Top_{cg}^{\ast/})_{Quillen}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{Maps(S^1, -)_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{S^1 \wedge (-)}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    (Top_{cg}^{\ast/})_{Quillen}
            %p
              of cor.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashHomAdjunctionOnPointedCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_78 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LoopingAsFunctorOnHomotopyCategory"}
              we may represent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              by any choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+objects"} cylinder objects
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+objects"} path space objects
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathAndCylinderObjectsInAModelCategory"}
            %p
              The standard topological path space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^I
              is generally a path space object by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalPathSpaceIsGoodPathSpaceObject"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedSuspensionBySmashProductWithCircle"}
              this shows that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega  \simeq  \mathbb{R} Maps(S^1,-)_\ast
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, by the existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-approximations"} CW-approximations
              (remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EveryTopologicalSpaceWeaklyEquivalentToACWComplex"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\times I
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalCylinderOnCWComplexIsGoodCylinderObject"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedSuspensionBySmashProductWithCircle"}
              this shows that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma \simeq \mathbb{L} (S^1 \wedge (-))
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#final_remark Final remark
            %p
              What is called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
              is the result of universally forcing the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma\dashv \Omega)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuspensionAndLoopAreAdjointOnHomotopyCategory"}
              to become an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p
            This is the topic of the next section at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory – 1
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#References References
          %p
            A concise and yet self-contained re-write of the proof (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            is provided in
          %ul
            %li#Hirschhorn15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"}> Philip Hirschhorn
              ,
              %em The Quillen model category of topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1508.01942"}> arXiv:1508.01942
              ).
          %p
            For general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            theory a decent review is in
          %ul
            %li#DwyerSpalinski95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              , J. Spalinski,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+theories+and+model+categories"} Homotopy theories and model categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/paularne/SUPh05/DS.pdf"}> pdf
              ) in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"} Ioan Mackenzie James
              (ed.),
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
              1995
          %p The equivalent definition of model categories that we use here is due to
          %ul
            %li#Joyal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              , appendix E of
              %em The theory of quasi-categories and its applications
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.crm.cat/HigherCategories/hc2.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p The two originals are still a good source to turn to:
          %ul
            %li#Quillen67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                ,
                %em Axiomatic homotopy theory
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopical algebra
            %li#Brown73
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"}> Kenneth Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abstract+Homotopy+Theory+and+Generalized+Sheaf+Cohomology"} Abstract Homotopy Theory and Generalized Sheaf Cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1996573"} JSTOR
          %p
            For the restriction to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            good sources are
          %ul
            %li#Lewis78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Gaunce+Lewis"}> L. Gaunce Lewis
                ,
                %em Compactly generated spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/MISC/GaunceApp.pdf"}> pdf
                ), appendix A of
                %em The Stable Category and Generalized Thom Spectra
                PhD thesis Chicago, 1978
            %li#Strickland09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"}> Neil Strickland
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The category of CGWH spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://neil-strickland.staff.shef.ac.uk/courses/homotopy/cgwh.pdf"} pdf
          %p Graphics taken from
          %ul
            %li#Muro10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Muro"}> Fernando Muro
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Representability of Cohomology Theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://personal.us.es/fmuro/files/slides/praha.pdf"} slides
        .revisedby
